cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ARutGIS: a free and open-source GIS with full Thai support, developed from RustGIS"
message: >-
  If you use ARutGIS, please cite it and also RustGIS, the project it is
  developed from (listed under references below).
type: software
abstract: >-
  ARutGIS is a free and open-source GIS with full Thai support (Thai interface,
  Thai text on maps, Thai coordinate systems and Thai land units), developed by
  Anirut Ladawadee from RustGIS by Qiusheng Wu and the RustGIS contributors,
  under the same Apache-2.0 licence. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by
  the RustGIS project.
authors:
  - given-names: Anirut
    family-names: Ladawadee
version: 0.5.8
date-released: 2026-11-09
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexrut99/ARutGIS"
url: "https://alexrut99.github.io/ARutGIS/"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - GIS
  - geospatial
  - Thai
  - Rust
  - WebAssembly
  - mapping
  - spatial analysis
references:
  - type: software
    title: "RustGIS: A fast, free and open-source GIS in pure Rust for mapping, analyzing and sharing geospatial data"
    abstract: >-
      The project ARutGIS is developed from: ARutGIS forked RustGIS's main branch
      on 2026-10-29 (commit 90576c52, after the 0.4.0 release). The DOI is the
      concept DOI of all RustGIS releases.
